{
  "//": [
    "THE CONTRAST DEBT LEDGER — what the shipping shell was ALREADY failing on 2026-08-30, the day",
    "contrast.js was built. It is NOT a list of things that are acceptable. Every entry is a real WCAG AA",
    "failure, computed and printed with its ratio on every run.",
    "",
    "It exists so that a red run means 'someone made this worse today' rather than 'this repository has",
    "old debt' — the second message is the one people learn to scroll past, and a gate people scroll past",
    "is a gate that is not there. A signature not in this file FAILS. A signature in this file whose ratio",
    "got worse FAILS. `cap` is what the ledger held when it was written, and check 13 refuses to let it",
    "grow past that, so the only direction is down.",
    "",
    "A signature is a COLOUR PAIRING at a size, not a node: `--ink-faint` on `--paper-rail` at 13.5px is",
    "one defect however many rail rows wear it. Fixing the token clears every entry that names it.",
    "",
    "`surfaceFloors` is the second half of the same idea, borrowed from run.js: how many nodes each",
    "surface driver reached when the floor was set. A driver that stops reaching its state would otherwise",
    "report a thinner walk as a cleaner one.",
    "",
    "`exemptionCap` is the number of `data-contrast-exempt` declarations the shipped source may carry.",
    "It is 0. Nothing in this app is currently claiming to be text nobody is meant to read, and raising",
    "the cap is a decision someone makes in the commit that adds the first one.",
    "",
    "`knownUnresolvable` is the shortest and most closely watched list here: colours the gate CANNOT PROVE.",
    "Not passing. Not excused. Written down so that the blind spot has a name, a node and a reason, and so",
    "that a new one fails the run instead of joining a silent pile."
